<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Astara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Astara is a town on the Caspian coast divided by the Astara river between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, the two halves forming separate towns. It was the first capital of the Talysh Khanate in the 18th century, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-turkmenchay">Treaty of Turkmenchay</a> of 1828 made the river the border between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. It is now a road and rail crossing between the two countries.</p></div>
